+# Detached Lab runtime integration
+
+AOS can opt in to bounded research jobs handled by a separate local Lab service. These jobs use the immutable `aos_external_jobs` ledger and the Lab loopback API; they do not enter `DesktopScheduler` and do not reserve its foreground task slot.
+
+## Explicit opt-in
+
+`scripts/serve_desktop.py` enables the integration only when all three options are supplied: `--lab-external-api-url`, `--lab-external-token-file`, and one or more repeated `--lab-external-suite` values. The API client accepts only an explicit loopback HTTP URL and a regular, user-owned mode-0600 token file. The token is read from that file and is never placed in process arguments or logs.
+
+The runtime also requires `--engine decider --reuse-decider --shared-gpu-turns`. Each authorized Lab start uses the configured Decider through the shared GPU broker. This is a local control-plane opt-in; it does not authorize public data, external model APIs, or a research suite that is absent from the explicit allowlist.
+
+Example argument shape (replace the URL, private file path, and suite ID with the local deployment's values):
+
+```text
+python scripts/serve_desktop.py --engine decider --reuse-decider --shared-gpu-turns \
+  --lab-external-api-url http://127.0.0.1:8788 \
+  --lab-external-token-file /run/user/1000/lab-api.token \
+  --lab-external-suite synthetic.allowed.v1
+```
+
+## Admission, authority, and restart
+
+- At most eight `dispatch_pending`, `queued`, `running`, or `stop_requested` Lab jobs may be active across the AOS ledger. Capacity is checked before model authorization and again inside the durable write transaction. Legacy active rows above the limit block new starts.
+- Identical concurrent requests with the same session and idempotency key share one authorization and dispatch. Reuse of an in-flight key with a different payload is rejected.
+- Start authorization runs without the desktop control lock or foreground scheduler slot. After inference, the coordinator checks the session, lease, generation, runtime, and typed action again. The five-second action deadline starts after the model decision.
+- `/api/restart/quiesce` closes Lab start admission, drains any in-flight start through durable handle binding, requests stop for every active job bound to the current session, and only then leaves restart quiesce enabled. A missing handle, failed stop, unresolved dispatch, or active job still bound to an older session fails the restart request closed. It does not silently ignore legacy rows after the eighth job.
+- A successful stop request pauses the corresponding AOS typed run. After a new desktop session and human lease exist, the authenticated Lab recovery endpoint can explicitly rebind an acknowledged active job; recovery never resubmits the start request. `/api/restart/release` reopens start admission only when a restart is explicitly cancelled in the same session.
+
+The integration's fixture and package tests establish software behavior only. A real shared-broker Decider turn and concurrent AOS/Lab GPU acceptance must be recorded separately in `docs/STATUS.md`.
