+# Detached Lab / shared broker — isolated current-source draft
+
+Prepared 2026-09-29 against source-only snapshot `0101ef6c806c` (1082 files,
+11,185,537 bytes). This is an isolated draft; live AOS was not changed and
+no model, GPU, desktop service or production database was launched.
+
+The Lab options remain explicit and all-or-none: a bounded loopback API,
+owner-only token file and exact suite allowlist. Typed start/status/stop/
+recover/report operations use a separate durable Lab job identity. Long
+research runs do not reserve the foreground desktop scheduler slot. Start
+and stop revalidate current session, lease and generation after awaited
+policy/model decisions; polling does not call an LLM. A verified report
+requires its independent canonical content hash before completion.
+
+Shared broker inference preserves current pin verification, readiness and
+bounded model profiles. CPU prewarm and retained GPU workers cannot be
+combined with broker opt-in. Current owned-skill planning has a separate
+Bonsai path and remains rejected with shared turns until explicitly
+adapted. The ordinary non-broker retention lifecycle remains available.
+Restart quiesces and drains only this session's detached Lab jobs; an
+unresolved drain leaves Lab admission closed while releasing the desktop
+quiesce. Existing scheduler planning, adaptation, sequence and restart
+locks are preserved.
+
+Migrations 0018/0019 follow the captured 0017 chain and are only applied to
+isolated test databases. The base manifest's two existing hash mismatches
+are preserved in capture evidence; the merged source manifest is freshly
+computed. Public broker worker source is included in package allowlisting.
+
+CPU fixture tests and package validation are recorded separately in the
+source-bound rebase receipt. They cannot prove real GPU fairness, actual
+research plus desktop coexistence, or permission to replace live AOS.
+Before live promotion, coordinate the parallel AOS owner and recheck current
+source hashes and migration names. The pending shared-GPU coordination
+condition remains in force.
